 "note": "Every colour a figure may wear, by name, with its source. The generator lays them out in this order as 16 px cells of one shared 256 x 256 palette texture (cp_palette_albedo.png, sRGB, no mips, point filter) and points each face's UV at the cell centre of its colour: one material for every figure and LOD. metal/smooth go into cp_palette_metal.png (R metallic, G occlusion 1, A smoothness) for the same cell. Brass is a thin line only (hem bands), never a panel. Amber and violet are world colours on cloth (GDD §15: signals don't own them). Round 2 (Glyph's read): the commuter block pool holds no yellow, orange or gold (guards) and no violet or magenta (rivals); commuters wear one block on a cream, ivory or ink base, never head to toe; guards a deeper amber over ivory or ink; cafe seafoam with a white apron and a chrome line, never peach. D is the dark step every figure carries (belt, yoke, band or boots).",
